  "lab_content": [
    {"lab_id":"l-1","media":["youtube:dQw4w9WgXcQ"],"content":"<h2>Objectives</h2><p>Determine the molarity of acetic acid in vinegar.</p><h2>Safety</h2><ul><li>Goggles on at all times.</li><li>NaOH is caustic; rinse spills immediately.</li></ul><h2>Procedure</h2><ol><li>Pipette 10.00 mL of vinegar into a flask.</li><li>Add two drops of phenolphthalein.</li><li>Titrate with $0.100\\ \\text{M}$ NaOH to the first persistent pink.</li></ol><p>The reaction is $$\\ce{CH3COOH + NaOH -> CH3COONa + H2O}$$ and the concentration follows from $$c_a = \\frac{c_b V_b}{V_a}$$</p>"},
    {"lab_id":"l-2","media":[],"content":"<p>Chop cabbage, boil, strain. Test with vinegar, baking soda and soap.</p>"},
    {"lab_id":"l-4","media":[],"content":"<h2>Rules</h2><ol><li>No food or drink.</li><li>Know where the eyewash station is.</li></ol>"}
